																	<article id="post-58445" class="post type-post status-publish">

	
		
            <div class="header-standard header-classic single-header">
								
				                <h1 class="post-title single-post-title entry-title">How To Make Dragon Cookies</h1>
																				                    <div class="post-box-meta-single">
						                            <span class="author-post byline"><span
                                        class="author vcard">written by                                         <a class="author-url url fn n" href="https://whattocooktoday.com/author/mgoh888">Marvellina</a>									</span>
                            </span>
																		                            <span><time class="entry-date published" datetime="2021-01-31T21:07:49-06:00"><span>Published:</span> January 31, 2021</time></span>
																														                    </div>
								            </div>

			
			
			
		
		
										
		
	
	
	
	    <div class="post-entry blockquote-style-1 ">
        <div class="inner-post-entry entry-content" id="penci-post-entry-inner">

			<i class="penci-post-countview-number-check" style="display:none">8.6K</i>
			
<div id="wpadc-wrapper" class="wpadc-wrapper-class wpadc-disclosure wpadc-selected-before-content wpadc-rule-101192">
<h6><em>This post may contain affiliate links. Please read our <a href="https://whattocooktoday.com/disclosure-and-privacy-policy">disclosure policy.</a></em></h6>
</div>
<p>		<strong>Fun to make dragon cookies by piping butter cookie dough. All the tips you need to know to make this successfully. The cookies are naturally gluten-free.</strong><br />
<img fetchpriority="high" decoding="async" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-58460" src="https://whattocooktoday.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/01/dragon-cookies-10.jpg" alt="Easy Dragon Cookies (Chinese New Year)" width="1200" height="1800" data-pin-description="Easy Dragon Cookies (Chinese New Year)" data-pin-title="Easy Dragon Cookies (Chinese New Year)" srcset="https://whattocooktoday.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/01/dragon-cookies-10.jpg 1200w, https://whattocooktoday.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/01/dragon-cookies-10-200x300.jpg 200w, https://whattocooktoday.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/01/dragon-cookies-10-683x1024.jpg 683w, https://whattocooktoday.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/01/dragon-cookies-10-768x1152.jpg 768w, https://whattocooktoday.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/01/dragon-cookies-10-1024x1536.jpg 1024w, https://whattocooktoday.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/01/dragon-cookies-10-1170x1755.jpg 1170w, https://whattocooktoday.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/01/dragon-cookies-10-585x878.jpg 585w" sizes="(max-width: 1200px) 100vw, 1200px" /></p><div class="wprm-recipe wprm-recipe-snippet wprm-recipe-template-jump-to-buttons"><a href="#recipe" data-recipe="58447" style="color: #000000;background-color: #ddf3ed;border-color: #ffffff;border-radius: 0px;padding: 5px 5px;" class="wprm-recipe-jump wprm-recipe-link wprm-jump-to-recipe-shortcode wprm-block-text-bold wprm-recipe-jump-wide-button wprm-recipe-link-wide-button wprm-color-accent"><span class="wprm-recipe-icon wprm-recipe-jump-icon"><svg width="16px" height="16px" viewBox="0 0 24 24" version="1.1" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"><g stroke="none" stroke-width="1" fill="none" fill-rule="evenodd"><g fill="#000000"><path d="M15.9199,4.9443 L18.1399,2.7243 C18.5509,2.3133 19.0909,2.1083 19.6299,2.1083 C20.1699,2.1083 20.7099,2.3133 21.1209,2.7243 C21.9429,3.5473 21.9419,4.8843 21.1209,5.7073 L18.9019,7.9253 C18.0799,8.7483 16.7419,8.7483 15.9199,7.9253 C15.0979,7.1033 15.0979,5.7663 15.9199,4.9443 M23.5529,22.1383 L13.3369,11.9233 L15.3109,9.9493 C15.9559,10.3353 16.6809,10.5413 17.4109,10.5413 C18.4629,10.5413 19.5159,10.1403 20.3159,9.3403 L22.5349,7.1213 C24.1369,5.5183 24.1369,2.9123 22.5349,1.3103 C21.7599,0.5343 20.7279,0.1073 19.6299,0.1073 C18.5329,0.1073 17.5019,0.5343 16.7259,1.3103 L14.5059,3.5303 C13.7299,4.3063 13.3029,5.3383 13.3029,6.4343 C13.3029,7.1883 13.5179,7.9053 13.8959,8.5363 L11.9229,10.5083 L9.9489,8.5353 C10.8909,6.9593 10.6959,4.8863 9.3399,3.5303 L6.1039,0.2933 C5.7129,-0.0977 5.0799,-0.0977 4.6899,0.2933 C4.2989,0.6833 4.2989,1.3163 4.6899,1.7073 L7.9259,4.9443 C8.4909,5.5093 8.6579,6.3153 8.4459,7.0323 L3.6539,2.2403 C3.2639,1.8493 2.6309,1.8493 2.2399,2.2403 C1.8499,2.6313 1.8499,3.2633 2.2399,3.6543 L7.0319,8.4463 C6.3149,8.6583 5.5089,8.4913 4.9429,7.9253 L1.7069,4.6893 C1.3159,4.2983 0.6839,4.2983 0.2929,4.6893 C-0.0981,5.0803 -0.0981,5.7133 0.2929,6.1033 L3.5289,9.3403 C4.3309,10.1403 5.3829,10.5413 6.4349,10.5413 C7.1649,10.5413 7.8899,10.3353 8.5349,9.9493 L10.5089,11.9233 L0.2929,22.1383 C-0.0981,22.5293 -0.0981,23.1623 0.2929,23.5523 C0.4879,23.7483 0.7439,23.8453 0.9999,23.8453 C1.2559,23.8453 1.5119,23.7483 1.7069,23.5523 L11.9229,13.3373 L22.1389,23.5523 C22.3339,23.7483 22.5899,23.8453 22.8459,23.8453 C23.1019,23.8453 23.3569,23.7483 23.5529,23.5523 C23.9429,23.1623 23.9429,22.5293 23.5529,22.1383"></path></g></g></svg></span> VIEW RECIPE </a>
<a href="#commentform" class="wprm-recipe-jump-to-comments wprm-recipe-link wprm-block-text-bold wprm-recipe-jump-to-comments-wide-button wprm-recipe-link-wide-button wprm-color-accent" style="color: #000000;background-color: #eef2f7;border-color: #ffffff;border-radius: 0px;padding: 5px 5px;"><span class="wprm-recipe-icon wprm-recipe-jump-to-comments-icon"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><g class="nc-icon-wrapper" fill="#000000"><path fill="#000000" d="M24,11c0-5.5-5.4-10-12-10S0,5.5,0,11s5.4,10,12,10c1,0,2-0.1,3-0.3l5.6,2.2c0.1,0,0.2,0.1,0.4,0.1 c0.2,0,0.4-0.1,0.6-0.2c0.3-0.2,0.4-0.6,0.4-0.9l-0.5-4.7C23.1,15.4,24,13.2,24,11z M14,14H7v-2h7V14z M17,10H7V8h10V10z"/></g></svg></span> COMMENTS</a>

</div>
<p>This year is not a dragon year, but <a href="https://whattocooktoday.com/the-year-of-ox-steamed-buns.html">the year of the ox</a>. Nevertheless, I made these dragon cookies because I had some leftover yolks and this was sort of a long-overdue little project I&#8217;ve been wanting to do even before Game of Throne ends a few years ago! If you watch Game of Throne you know there were dragons in there. Anyway, after few years of delays, so here I am LOL!</p>
<h2><strong>The recipe rundown</strong></h2>
<p><strong>Taste:</strong> They are like butter cookies. Sweet (though my kids said could be sweeter) and buttery<br />
<strong>Texture:</strong> Crisp on the edge and soft inside<br />
<strong>Level:</strong> Medium<br />
<strong>Pros:</strong> They are fun to make and you don&#8217;t need kitchen gadget like a mixer<br />
<strong>Cons:</strong> Getting the right dough consistency can be the challenge here. I have failed 3 times before I figure it out</p>
<h2><strong>So, I failed three times before this</strong></h2>
<p>The dough consistency is important here. The right balance between the butter, the cornstarch, the sugar, and the egg yolks,hey.. pretty much the entire recipe 🙂<br />
<strong>My first attempt:</strong> the cookies literally melt into large thin butter cookies during baking LOL! The dough is too fluid and soft.<br />
<strong>My second attempt:</strong> the cookie dough was almost impossible to pipe through the nozzle. I literally squeeze SOO..HARD&#8230;and it&#8217;s like the dough is constipated. I just threw the whole thing away<br />
<strong>My third attempt:</strong> the cookie dough was more manageable but the taste was off. It tasted so starchy (too much cornstarch)<br />
<strong>My fourth attempt (the photos you are seeing here)</strong>: The cookie dough is soft enough to pipe with a bit of resistance, but it should be pipeable without having to squeeze so hard! It tastes the best among all, probably can be a bit sweeter? but this is subjective I suppose!</p>
<p><img decoding="async" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-58465" src="https://whattocooktoday.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/01/dragon-cookies-15.jpg" alt="Easy Dragon Cookies (Chinese New Year)" width="1200" height="800" data-pin-description="Easy Dragon Cookies (Chinese New Year)" data-pin-title="Easy Dragon Cookies (Chinese New Year)" srcset="https://whattocooktoday.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/01/dragon-cookies-15.jpg 1200w, https://whattocooktoday.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/01/dragon-cookies-15-300x200.jpg 300w, https://whattocooktoday.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/01/dragon-cookies-15-1024x683.jpg 1024w, https://whattocooktoday.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/01/dragon-cookies-15-768x512.jpg 768w, https://whattocooktoday.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/01/dragon-cookies-15-1170x780.jpg 1170w, https://whattocooktoday.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/01/dragon-cookies-15-585x390.jpg 585w, https://whattocooktoday.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/01/dragon-cookies-15-263x175.jpg 263w" sizes="(max-width: 1200px) 100vw, 1200px" /></p>
<h2><strong>How To Make Dragon Cookies</strong></h2>
<p>1. Soften the butter at room temperature. I cut it intso smaller pieces and leave it out for about 30 minutes.You should be able to easily mash it with a wooden spatula or the back of a spoon<br />
<img decoding="async" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-58451" src="https://whattocooktoday.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/01/dragon-cookies-1.jpg" alt="" width="450" height="300" srcset="https://whattocooktoday.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/01/dragon-cookies-1.jpg 450w, https://whattocooktoday.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/01/dragon-cookies-1-300x200.jpg 300w, https://whattocooktoday.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/01/dragon-cookies-1-263x175.jpg 263w" sizes="(max-width: 450px) 100vw, 450px" /><br />
2. Mash the butter and then add icing sugar and combine until the icing sugar is no longer visible<br />
<img loading="lazy" decoding="async" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-58452" src="https://whattocooktoday.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/01/dragon-cookies-2.jpg" alt="" width="450" height="300" srcset="https://whattocooktoday.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/01/dragon-cookies-2.jpg 450w, https://whattocooktoday.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/01/dragon-cookies-2-300x200.jpg 300w, https://whattocooktoday.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/01/dragon-cookies-2-263x175.jpg 263w" sizes="(max-width: 450px) 100vw, 450px" /><br />
3. Add vanilla and egg yolks (I highly recommend you actually weigh the egg yolks as this determines the consistency of the cookie dough) and stir again to combine until creamy<br />
<img loading="lazy" decoding="async" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-58453" src="https://whattocooktoday.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/01/dragon-cookies-3.jpg" alt="" width="450" height="300" srcset="https://whattocooktoday.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/01/dragon-cookies-3.jpg 450w, https://whattocooktoday.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/01/dragon-cookies-3-300x200.jpg 300w, https://whattocooktoday.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/01/dragon-cookies-3-263x175.jpg 263w" sizes="(max-width: 450px) 100vw, 450px" /></p>
<p><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-58454" src="https://whattocooktoday.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/01/dragon-cookies-4.jpg" alt="" width="450" height="300" srcset="https://whattocooktoday.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/01/dragon-cookies-4.jpg 450w, https://whattocooktoday.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/01/dragon-cookies-4-300x200.jpg 300w, https://whattocooktoday.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/01/dragon-cookies-4-263x175.jpg 263w" sizes="(max-width: 450px) 100vw, 450px" /><br />
4. Sift in the dry ingredients. Combine until you get a soft dough and slightly sticky. The dough needs to be soft enough so you can pipe through the nozzle<br />
<img loading="lazy" decoding="async" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-58455" src="https://whattocooktoday.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/01/dragon-cookies-5.jpg" alt="" width="450" height="300" srcset="https://whattocooktoday.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/01/dragon-cookies-5.jpg 450w, https://whattocooktoday.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/01/dragon-cookies-5-300x200.jpg 300w, https://whattocooktoday.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/01/dragon-cookies-5-263x175.jpg 263w" sizes="(max-width: 450px) 100vw, 450px" /><br />
5. If you want to color the dough, divide the dough into two and put a small drop of color on one of them and knead the dough to even out the color<br />
<img loading="lazy" decoding="async" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-58458" src="https://whattocooktoday.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/01/dragon-cookies-8.jpg" alt="" width="450" height="300" srcset="https://whattocooktoday.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/01/dragon-cookies-8.jpg 450w, https://whattocooktoday.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/01/dragon-cookies-8-300x200.jpg 300w, https://whattocooktoday.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/01/dragon-cookies-8-263x175.jpg 263w" sizes="(max-width: 450px) 100vw, 450px" /><br />
6. I use Wilton 1M tip because I think it makes rougher scales(more &#8220;crackly&#8221;) compared to when I use Wilton 4B. My son said it looked more like a dragon (though he still thinks it&#8217;s more like a snake than dragon LOL). Anyway, it&#8217;s up to you</p>
<div id="attachment_58457" style="width: 460px" class="wp-caption aligncenter"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" aria-describedby="caption-attachment-58457" class="size-full wp-image-58457" src="https://whattocooktoday.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/01/dragon-cookies-7.jpg" alt="Wilton 1M tip" width="450" height="300" data-pin-description="Wilton 1M tip" data-pin-title="Wilton 1M tip" srcset="https://whattocooktoday.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/01/dragon-cookies-7.jpg 450w, https://whattocooktoday.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/01/dragon-cookies-7-300x200.jpg 300w, https://whattocooktoday.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/01/dragon-cookies-7-263x175.jpg 263w" sizes="(max-width: 450px) 100vw, 450px" /><p id="caption-attachment-58457" class="wp-caption-text">Wilton 1M tip</p></div>
<p>7. Pipe almost like an &#8220;S&#8221; letter. You don&#8217;t want to pipe too long as it will look more like a snake. You can pipe about 1/2 inch apart, the cookie spread a little but not a whole lot. After you are done piping, chill the whole tray inside the freezer (yes,freezer) for at least 30 minutes. This helps to maintain their shapes<br />
<img loading="lazy" decoding="async" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-58459" src="https://whattocooktoday.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/01/dragon-cookies-9.jpg" alt="" width="450" height="300" srcset="https://whattocooktoday.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/01/dragon-cookies-9.jpg 450w, https://whattocooktoday.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/01/dragon-cookies-9-300x200.jpg 300w, https://whattocooktoday.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/01/dragon-cookies-9-263x175.jpg 263w" sizes="(max-width: 450px) 100vw, 450px" /><br />
8. 15 minutes before the end of time, preheat the oven to 320 F (160 C). Put the tray in the middle of the oven and bake for 15-18 minutes<br />
<img loading="lazy" decoding="async" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-58468" src="https://whattocooktoday.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/01/dragon-cookies-16.jpg" alt="" width="450" height="300" srcset="https://whattocooktoday.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/01/dragon-cookies-16.jpg 450w, https://whattocooktoday.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/01/dragon-cookies-16-300x200.jpg 300w, https://whattocooktoday.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/01/dragon-cookies-16-263x175.jpg 263w" sizes="(max-width: 450px) 100vw, 450px" /><br />
9. The cookies shouldn&#8217;t brown much, just slightly golden brown at the bottom<br />
<img loading="lazy" decoding="async" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-58470" src="https://whattocooktoday.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/01/dragon-cookies-18.jpg" alt="" width="450" height="300" srcset="https://whattocooktoday.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/01/dragon-cookies-18.jpg 450w, https://whattocooktoday.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/01/dragon-cookies-18-300x200.jpg 300w, https://whattocooktoday.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/01/dragon-cookies-18-263x175.jpg 263w" sizes="(max-width: 450px) 100vw, 450px" /><br />
10. Remove from the oven and let them cool on the tray for 10 minutes<br />
<img loading="lazy" decoding="async" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-58469" src="https://whattocooktoday.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/01/dragon-cookies-17.jpg" alt="" width="450" height="300" srcset="https://whattocooktoday.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/01/dragon-cookies-17.jpg 450w, https://whattocooktoday.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/01/dragon-cookies-17-300x200.jpg 300w, https://whattocooktoday.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/01/dragon-cookies-17-263x175.jpg 263w" sizes="(max-width: 450px) 100vw, 450px" /><br />
11. Transfer to a cooling rack to let them cool down completely. Dip the blunt tip of a toothpick in a red food coloring to dot the eyes<br />
<img loading="lazy" decoding="async" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-58471" src="https://whattocooktoday.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/01/dragon-cookies-19.jpg" alt="" width="450" height="300" srcset="https://whattocooktoday.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/01/dragon-cookies-19.jpg 450w, https://whattocooktoday.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/01/dragon-cookies-19-300x200.jpg 300w, https://whattocooktoday.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/01/dragon-cookies-19-263x175.jpg 263w" sizes="(max-width: 450px) 100vw, 450px" /><br />
<img loading="lazy" decoding="async" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-58472" src="https://whattocooktoday.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/01/dragon-cookies-20.jpg" alt="" width="450" height="300" srcset="https://whattocooktoday.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/01/dragon-cookies-20.jpg 450w, https://whattocooktoday.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/01/dragon-cookies-20-300x200.jpg 300w, https://whattocooktoday.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/01/dragon-cookies-20-263x175.jpg 263w" sizes="(max-width: 450px) 100vw, 450px" /></p>
<p>So the family agrees that this version tasted the best and looked the best as they can be (though not perfect!).<br />
<img loading="lazy" decoding="async" data-pin-description="Easy Dragon Cookies (Chinese New Year)" data-pin-title="Easy Dragon Cookies (Chinese New Year)" src="https://whattocooktoday.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/01/dragon-cookies-10.jpg" alt="Easy Dragon Cookies (Chinese New Year)" width="1200" height="1800" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-58460" srcset="https://whattocooktoday.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/01/dragon-cookies-10.jpg 1200w, https://whattocooktoday.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/01/dragon-cookies-10-200x300.jpg 200w, https://whattocooktoday.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/01/dragon-cookies-10-683x1024.jpg 683w, https://whattocooktoday.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/01/dragon-cookies-10-768x1152.jpg 768w, https://whattocooktoday.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/01/dragon-cookies-10-1024x1536.jpg 1024w, https://whattocooktoday.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/01/dragon-cookies-10-1170x1755.jpg 1170w, https://whattocooktoday.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/01/dragon-cookies-10-585x878.jpg 585w" sizes="(max-width: 1200px) 100vw, 1200px" /></p>
<h2><strong>Tips for success</strong></h2>
<p>1. Make sure you use durable piping bag. A quality that you know won&#8217;t burst easily if you squeeze<br />
2. I recommend using Wilton 1M or something similar from another brand versus Wilton 4B, but it&#8217;s a personal preference<br />
3. I recommend weighing the egg yolk for precision if possible, as this affects the consistency of the dough<br />
4. You need to chill the piped cookie dough in the freezer for at least 30 minutes<br />
 <img loading="lazy" decoding="async" data-pin-description="Easy Dragon Cookies (Chinese New Year)" data-pin-title="Easy Dragon Cookies (Chinese New Year)" src="https://whattocooktoday.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/01/dragon-cookies-13.jpg" alt="Easy Dragon Cookies (Chinese New Year)" width="1200" height="1800" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-58463" srcset="https://whattocooktoday.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/01/dragon-cookies-13.jpg 1200w, https://whattocooktoday.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/01/dragon-cookies-13-200x300.jpg 200w, https://whattocooktoday.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/01/dragon-cookies-13-683x1024.jpg 683w, https://whattocooktoday.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/01/dragon-cookies-13-768x1152.jpg 768w, https://whattocooktoday.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/01/dragon-cookies-13-1024x1536.jpg 1024w, https://whattocooktoday.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/01/dragon-cookies-13-1170x1755.jpg 1170w, https://whattocooktoday.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/01/dragon-cookies-13-585x878.jpg 585w" sizes="(max-width: 1200px) 100vw, 1200px" /></p>
<h2><strong>Did you make this recipe?</strong></h2>
<p>I love it when you guys snap a photo and tag to show me what you&#8217;ve made 🙂 Simply tag me <strong>@WhatToCookToday #WhatToCookToday</strong> on <a href="https://www.instagram.com/whattocooktoday/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Instagram</a> and I&#8217;ll be sure to stop by and take a peek for real!<br />
<img loading="lazy" decoding="async" data-pin-description="Easy Dragon Cookies (Chinese New Year)" data-pin-title="Easy Dragon Cookies (Chinese New Year)" src="https://whattocooktoday.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/01/dragon-cookies-11.jpg" alt="Easy Dragon Cookies (Chinese New Year)" width="1200" height="1800" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-58461" srcset="https://whattocooktoday.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/01/dragon-cookies-11.jpg 1200w, https://whattocooktoday.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/01/dragon-cookies-11-200x300.jpg 200w, https://whattocooktoday.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/01/dragon-cookies-11-683x1024.jpg 683w, https://whattocooktoday.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/01/dragon-cookies-11-768x1152.jpg 768w, https://whattocooktoday.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/01/dragon-cookies-11-1024x1536.jpg 1024w, https://whattocooktoday.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/01/dragon-cookies-11-1170x1755.jpg 1170w, https://whattocooktoday.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/01/dragon-cookies-11-585x878.jpg 585w" sizes="(max-width: 1200px) 100vw, 1200px" /><br />
